424	   *      any port, that FIFO is alive; if NONE clears, the whole FIFO
425	   *      write path is dead (clock/gate/reset at the FIFO subsystem level).
426	   *
427	   *  (C) Does DAC_ENABLE gate the FPORT write?  We write DAC_FPORT with
428	   *      DAC_ENABLE=1, record status, then clear DAC_ENABLE and write
429	   *      again.  If status is identical either way, ENABLE does not gate
430	   *      the FIFO input — pointing at the FIFO subsystem, not the DAC.
